WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.177
Yes 17M lines

00:00:01.989 --> 00:00:02.684
of Lean is

00:00:02.496 --> 00:00:03.109
a lot

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.151
The Lean formalization

00:00:04.986 --> 00:00:06.200
effort now spans

00:00:06.012 --> 00:00:07.545
17 million lines

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.276
a look at

00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:09.125
what that scale

00:00:08.996 --> 00:00:10.104
actually means for

00:00:09.915 --> 00:00:11.413
a machine-checked proof

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:12.751
With the Lean

00:00:12.563 --> 00:00:13.872
formalization of the

00:00:13.683 --> 00:00:15.027
Riemann Hypothesis

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:16.313
manuscript now running

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:17.374
to 17 million

00:00:17.186 --> 00:00:17.799
lines

00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:19.060
this post puts

00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:19.791
that scale in

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:21.301
perspective and explains

00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:21.914
why the count

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.964
is so large

00:00:23.486 --> 00:00:24.205
Yes

00:00:24.241 --> 00:00:25.526
17m lines of

00:00:25.337 --> 00:00:26.151
Lean is a

00:00:25.962 --> 00:00:26.917
lot The recent

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:27.436
proof of the

00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:28.568
Riemann hypothesis

00:00:28.616 --> 00:00:29.252
came with a

00:00:29.064 --> 00:00:30.372
statistic attached

00:00:30.585 --> 00:00:31.398
the proof is

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.660
17 million lines

00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:33.179
of Lean

00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:34.716
Full story on

00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:35.423
the dashboard
